  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The velocity of a small ball of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;and density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cc</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> when dropped in a container filled with glycerine becomes constant after some time. If the density of glycerine is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cc</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then the value of viscous force acting on the ball will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .</p><p>[use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;be the viscous force and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;be the buoyant force acting on the ball.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0081_ac1aca0bd2ef.png\" style=\"width: 134px; height: 180px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>Then, when body moves with constant velocity,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>Or,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&rho;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mi>Vg</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&rho;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub><mi>Vg</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&rho;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&rho;</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>V</mi><mi>g</mi></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;is the volume of small ball.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&times;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&times;</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>67</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p>Thus, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}